# [[.DisplayName]]

Multi-stack workspace generated by [arlox](https://github.com/sureshmopidevi/arlox) **v[[.ArloxVersion]]**.

## Open

The `.code-workspace` file works in **Cursor**, **VS Code**, and **Antigravity IDE** (and other VS Code–compatible editors).

From the parent directory:

```bash
cursor --classic [[.Name]]/[[.Name]].code-workspace   # Cursor IDE (not Agents window)
code [[.Name]]/[[.Name]].code-workspace
agy-ide [[.Name]]/[[.Name]].code-workspace
```

Or from inside this project:

```bash
cursor --classic [[.Name]].code-workspace
code [[.Name]].code-workspace
agy-ide [[.Name]].code-workspace
```

You can also use **File → Open Workspace from File…** and pick `[[.Name]].code-workspace`.

Each of `backend/`, `web/`, and `app/` is its **own git repository**.

## Quick start (root Makefile)

From this folder:

```bash
make help      # all commands (backend.*, web.*, app.*)
make status    # which stacks exist
make dev       # starts backend, waits for /health/live, then web dev server
make app.run   # Flutter — run in its own terminal
```

Missing stacks are skipped automatically. Add more with `arlox add` (setup runs automatically for new stacks).

## Stacks

| Stack | Path | Run |
|-------|------|-----|
| Backend (Go + Gin) | `backend/` | `make backend.run` |
| Web (React + Tailwind) | `web/` | `make web.dev` |
| App (Flutter) | `app/` | `make app.run` |

Only folders that exist were generated. Add more later:

```bash
arlox add
```

## Database (Postgres)

```bash
make db-up          # Docker Postgres (project-specific host port)
make backend.setup
```

Host port is assigned from your project name (see `docker-compose.yml` and `backend/configs/local/app.env` — typically 5433–7432). Each workspace gets its own port so multiple projects can run Postgres at once.

## Full-stack features

Use `.cursor/skills/add-feature-fullstack` so agents implement **backend → web → app** sequentially (never in parallel for the same feature).

## Agent guardrails

Each stack ships `.cursor/rules` and `.cursor/skills` (architecture, Karpathy guidelines, `add-feature-backend` / `add-feature-web` / `add-feature-mobile` with `learned/` auto-log). See each stack’s `AGENTS.md`.
